#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/test-snapd-fixes.md:2
msgid "Test snapd fixes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/test-snapd-fixes.md:4
msgid ""
"The snap daemon, _snapd_, is the background service that manages and "
"maintains your snaps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/test-snapd-fixes.md:6
msgid ""
"Occasionally, _snapd_ may develop an issue or bug that is only apparent on "
"specific devices or in specific circumstances. A fix will be developed as "
"soon as possible, but we may need to test a fix on those devices or "
"installations before it can be merged and more widely distributed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/test-snapd-fixes.md:8
msgid ""
"In such cases, a patched _snapd_ can be provided via a pull request and "
"installed by those affected so they can report on whether it solves the "
"original issue. This process is outlined below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/test-snapd-fixes.md:10
msgid "Access GitHub"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/test-snapd-fixes.md:12
msgid ""
"The snap daemon, and its associated tools and projects are hosted on [GitHub]"
"(https://github.com/). The [snapd repository](https://github.com/canonical/"
"snapd) contains all the branches, pull requests, automated tests and "
"discussions applicable to _snapd_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/test-snapd-fixes.md:14
msgid ""
"A fix will typically be contained within a [pull request](https://"
"docs.github.com/en/pull-requests/collaborating-with-pull-requests/proposing-"
"changes-to-your-work-with-pull-requests/about-pull-requests) prior to it "
"being merged. The _snapd_ repository is configured to automatically test and "
"build an approved pull request, creating what is called an _artifact_ that "
"can be downloaded and tested locally."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/test-snapd-fixes.md:16
msgid ""
"A test release, especially from a pull request, should only be installed in "
"a test environment as its behaviour could obviously be unpredictable. To "
"install a test release, you will first need a GitHub account and you will "
"need to be logged in from your favourite web browser."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/test-snapd-fixes.md:18
msgid "Locate the pull request"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/test-snapd-fixes.md:20
msgid ""
"This location of the pull request will usually have been communicated "
"separately, but open pull requests can be found linked to from the _snapd_ "
"repository ([https://github.com/canonical/snapd/pulls](https://github.com/"
"canonical/snapd/pulls)). Each pull request has a unique number identifier, "
"such as `#11085`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/test-snapd-fixes.md:22
msgid ""
"With the pull request opened in your web browser, select the _Checks_ tab. "
"This contains the output from the automated tests and build processes "
"initiated when an approved pull request is created or updated. If a pull "
"request has only recently been submitted or updated, it can take some time "
"for this page to become fully populated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/test-snapd-fixes.md:24
msgid "![image|669x453](/images/access-github.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/test-snapd-fixes.md:24
#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/test-snapd-fixes.md:30
msgid "image|669x453"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/test-snapd-fixes.md:26
msgid "Download the artifact"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/test-snapd-fixes.md:28
msgid ""
"Select _Tests_ from the menu on the left. This will take you to the "
"_Actions_ tab for the snapd repository showing the test runs for the "
"previously selected pull request. Scroll to the bottom of this list and "
"you'll see the _artifacts_ section containing a link to the downloadable "
"`snap-files` zip archive (GitHub stores build logs and artifacts for 90 "
"days):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/test-snapd-fixes.md:30
msgid "![image|669x453](/images/download-artefact.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/test-snapd-fixes.md:32
msgid "Click on _snap-files_ to download the archive."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/test-snapd-fixes.md:34
msgid "Install the test version"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/test-snapd-fixes.md:36
msgid "First, unzip the file we downloaded:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/test-snapd-fixes.md:38
msgid ""
"$ unzip snap-files.zip\n"
"Archive:  snap-files.zip\n"
"  inflating: snapd_2.53.2+git6345be5.6345be5-dirty_amd64.snap\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/test-snapd-fixes.md:44
msgid ""
"This resultant snap for the specific pull request we selected earlier can "
"now be installed with snap's {ref}`dangerous mode <ref-install-"
"modes_dangerous-mode>`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/test-snapd-fixes.md:46
msgid ""
"$ snap install --dangerous snapd_2.53.2+git6345be5.6345be5-dirty_amd64.snap\n"
"2021-11-24T13:06:46Z INFO Waiting for automatic snapd restart...\n"
"snapd 2.53.2+git6345be5.6345be5-dirty installed\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/test-snapd-fixes.md:52
msgid ""
"At this point, the fix for the issue or bug can now be tested and the "
"results reported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/test-snapd-fixes.md:54
msgid ""
"To revert the local installation to an official _snapd_ release, simply "
"refresh the _snapd_ snap to its stable channel:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/test-snapd-fixes.md:56
msgid "$ snap refresh snapd --stable --amend\n"
msgstr ""
